      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract / supply-chain",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Stabble's discovery that a former North Korean employee had worked on its codebase — prompting an emergency LP withdrawal — illustrates that DEX smart-contract risk now includes adversarial insider access at the developer layer, not just audit gaps.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity / impermanent loss",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Concentrated-liquidity and exotic LP-less designs (Tangent, Curve v2-style on SUI) reduce capital inefficiency but amplify impermanent-loss exposure during sharp price moves, a risk most retail LPs underestimate.",
          "source": "https://www.coinbase.com/learn/crypto-glossary/what-is-impermanent-loss"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / memecoin volume distortion",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "PumpSwap hitting $10B in volume within ten days of launch, driven almost entirely by memecoin presale activity, shows that headline DEX volume figures can be dominated by ephemeral, high-churn flow that evaporates when speculative interest fades.",
          "source": "https://cryptorank.io/insights/analytics/amm-vs-order-book-dexs"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Single-chain DEX dominance (Hyperliquid capturing order-book market share, Firefly as a Manta-exclusive venue) creates ecosystem concentration where one chain's outage or exploit cascades into the DEX's entire liquidity base.",
          "source": "https://bitcoinfoundation.org/news/opinion/cex-vs-dex-which-crypto-exchange-is-better-in-2026-pros-cons-and-hidden-risks/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The Trader Joe grocery-chain trademark suit against the Avalanche DEX demonstrates that off-chain IP law is an underappreciated legal vector for DeFi protocols, independent of securities regulation.",
